<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>Slack-Based LMS — Sally May Saclauso</title>
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>
    *,*::before,*::after{margin:0;padding:0;box-sizing:border-box}
    :root{--bg:#fafafa;--surface:#fff;--text:#1a1a1a;--text-secondary:#6b7280;--accent:#2563eb;--accent-light:#eff6ff;--border:#e5e7eb;--radius:12px;--shadow-sm:0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.04);--shadow-md:0 4px 16px rgba(0,0,0,.06);--max-width:760px}
    html{scroll-behavior:smooth}
    body{font-family:'Inter',-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,sans-serif;background:var(--bg);color:var(--text);line-height:1.7;font-size:15px;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased}
    nav{position:fixed;top:0;left:0;right:0;z-index:100;background:rgba(250,250,250,.85);backdrop-filter:blur(12px);border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}
    nav .nav-inner{max-width:var(--max-width);margin:0 auto;padding:0 24px;height:56px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between}
    nav .logo{font-weight:700;font-size:16px;letter-spacing:-.3px;text-decoration:none;color:var(--text)}
    nav .back-link{font-size:13px;font-weight:500;color:var(--text-secondary);text-decoration:none;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;transition:color .2s}
    nav .back-link:hover{color:var(--accent)}
    .hero-section{padding-top:120px;padding-bottom:56px;max-width:var(--max-width);margin:0 auto;padding-left:24px;padding-right:24px}
    .project-label{font-size:11px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:1.5px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--accent);margin-bottom:12px}
    .hero-section h1{font-size:34px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.8px;line-height:1.2;margin-bottom:16px}
    .hero-section .subtitle{font-size:17px;color:var(--text-secondary);max-width:600px;margin-bottom:24px}
    .tags{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px;margin-bottom:8px}
    .tag{font-size:11px;font-weight:500;padding:4px 10px;border-radius:20px;letter-spacing:.2px}
    .tag.blue{background:#eff6ff;color:#2563eb}.tag.green{background:#ecfdf5;color:#059669}.tag.purple{background:#f5f3ff;color:#7c3aed}.tag.orange{background:#fff7ed;color:#ea580c}.tag.pink{background:#fdf2f8;color:#db2777}.tag.gray{background:#f3f4f6;color:#4b5563}
    .divider{max-width:var(--max-width);margin:0 auto;padding:0 24px}
    .divider hr{border:none;border-top:1px solid var(--border)}
    section{max-width:var(--max-width);margin:0 auto;padding:56px 24px}
    section h2{font-size:22px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.3px;margin-bottom:16px}
    section p{color:var(--text-secondary);margin-bottom:16px}
    .card{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);padding:28px 32px;margin-bottom:16px;box-shadow:var(--shadow-sm)}
    .card h3{font-size:16px;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:8px}
    .card p{margin-bottom:0}
    .two-col{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:16px}
    .feature-list{list-style:none;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px}
    .feature-list li{padding:16px 20px;background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);font-size:14px;display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:10px}
    .feature-list li .num{font-weight:700;color:var(--accent);min-width:24px}
    .stat-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:16px}
    .stat{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);padding:24px;text-align:center}
    .stat .value{font-size:28px;font-weight:700;color:var(--accent);margin-bottom:4px}
    .stat .label{font-size:12px;color:var(--text-secondary);font-weight:500}
    .process-step{display:flex;gap:20px;align-items:flex-start;margin-bottom:20px}
    .step-marker{width:36px;height:36px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--accent-light);color:var(--accent);font-weight:700;font-size:14px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;flex-shrink:0;margin-top:2px}
    .step-content h4{font-size:15px;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:4px}
    .step-content p{font-size:14px;color:var(--text-secondary);margin:0}
    .cta-box{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);padding:40px;text-align:center}
    .cta-box h2{margin-bottom:8px}
    .cta-box p{max-width:400px;margin:0 auto 20px}
    .btn{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;padding:10px 22px;border-radius:8px;font-size:14px;font-weight:500;text-decoration:none;transition:all .2s}
    .btn-primary{background:var(--accent);color:#fff}
    .btn-primary:hover{background:#1d4ed8;transform:translateY(-1px);box-shadow:var(--shadow-md)}
    footer{text-align:center;padding:32px 24px;font-size:12px;color:var(--text-secondary);border-top:1px solid var(--border)}
    .fade-in{opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px);transition:opacity .6s ease,transform .6s ease}
    .fade-in.visible{opacity:1;transform:translateY(0)}
    @media(max-width:640px){.hero-section{padding-top:100px}.hero-section h1{font-size:26px}.two-col,.stat-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <nav><div class="nav-inner">
    <a href="index.html" class="logo">Sally May Saclauso</a>
    <a href="index.html#projects" class="back-link">&larr; All Projects</a>
  </div></nav>

  <div class="hero-section">
    <div class="project-label">Project 01</div>
    <h1>Slack-Based LMS for Operations Training</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">A complete learning management system built on Airtable and delivered through Slack — enabling asynchronous, self-paced operations training with built-in quality assurance.</p>
    <div class="tags">
      <span class="tag blue">Airtable</span>
      <span class="tag green">Slack</span>
      <span class="tag purple">LMS Design</span>
      <span class="tag orange">QA System</span>
      <span class="tag gray">Operations</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="divider"><hr/></div>

  <!-- PROBLEM -->
  <section class="fade-in">
    <h2>The Problem</h2>
    <p>Operations teams often lack structured, repeatable training systems. Knowledge lives in scattered documents, onboarding is inconsistent, and there's no way to measure whether learners actually absorb mission-critical procedures. Traditional LMS platforms are expensive, over-engineered, and disconnected from where teams actually work — Slack.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="divider"><hr/></div>

  <!-- SOLUTION -->
  <section class="fade-in">
    <h2>The Solution</h2>
    <p>I designed and built a Slack-native LMS entirely on Airtable — 8 interconnected tables that manage the full learning lifecycle from course creation through learner completion, with quality assurance baked in at every stage.</p>
    <div class="two-col">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>For Trainers</h3>
        <p>Structured lesson authoring with hooks, core content, insights, takeaways, and missions. Built-in QA scoring, brand compliance checks, and revision tracking.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>For Learners</h3>
        <p>Bite-sized lessons delivered asynchronously through Slack threads. Clear objectives, difficulty levels, and mission-based verification to confirm understanding.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="divider"><hr/></div>

  <!-- ARCHITECTURE -->
  <section class="fade-in">
    <h2>System Architecture</h2>
    <p>The LMS is structured as 8 relational tables in Airtable, each serving a distinct purpose:</p>
    <ul class="feature-list">
      <li><span class="num">1</span><div><strong>Courses</strong> — top-level containers with status, difficulty range, completion rates, and average QA scores.</div></li>
      <li><span class="num">2</span><div><strong>Modules</strong> — thematic groupings within courses tracking published/draft/revision lesson counts and QA pass rates.</div></li>
      <li><span class="num">3</span><div><strong>Lessons</strong> — the core content table with 25+ fields: topic, objective, hook, core content, insight, takeaway, mission, verification, and tone presets.</div></li>
      <li><span class="num">4</span><div><strong>Lesson QA Records</strong> — quality gate with scores, verdicts, revision counts, priority flags, and golden example markers.</div></li>
      <li><span class="num">5</span><div><strong>Lesson Metrics</strong> — word counts by section, brand compliance scores, and PED flag tracking.</div></li>
      <li><span class="num">6</span><div><strong>Learners</strong> — user profiles with enrollment, current module, progress percentage, and status tracking.</div></li>
      <li><span class="num">7</span><div><strong>Lesson Submissions</strong> — individual learner submissions with scores, timestamps, and completion methods.</div></li>
      <li><span class="num">8</span><div><strong>Slack Threads</strong> — the delivery layer linking lesson content to actual Slack thread text for posting.</div></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <div class="divider"><hr/></div>

  <!-- PROCESS -->
  <section class="fade-in">
    <h2>Process &amp; Workflow</h2>
    <div class="process-step">
      <div class="step-marker">1</div>
      <div class="step-content"><h4>Course &amp; Module Design</h4><p>Defined learning objectives, structured multi-month courses into weekly modules with progressive difficulty tiers.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="process-step">
      <div class="step-marker">2</div>
      <div class="step-content"><h4>Lesson Authoring</h4><p>Created each lesson with a structured format: hook to grab attention, core content for the main teaching, an insight for deeper thinking, a takeaway for retention, and a mission for hands-on practice.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="process-step">
      <div class="step-marker">3</div>
      <div class="step-content"><h4>Quality Assurance</h4><p>Each lesson goes through QA scoring — checking brand compliance, word counts, difficulty calibration, and content accuracy. Lessons below threshold get flagged for revision.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="process-step">
      <div class="step-marker">4</div>
      <div class="step-content"><h4>Slack Delivery</h4><p>Approved lessons are formatted into Slack thread text and posted to training channels. Learners engage asynchronously at their own pace.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="process-step">
      <div class="step-marker">5</div>
      <div class="step-content"><h4>Tracking &amp; Iteration</h4><p>Learner submissions are scored and tracked. Completion rates, QA scores, and engagement metrics feed back into course improvement.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="divider"><hr/></div>

  <!-- RESULTS -->
  <section class="fade-in">
    <h2>Results &amp; Impact</h2>
    <div class="stat-grid">
      <div class="stat"><div class="value">8</div><div class="label">Relational Tables</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="value">25+</div><div class="label">Fields per Lesson</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="value">100%</div><div class="label">Async Delivery</div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="divider"><hr/></div>

  <!-- TOOLS -->
  <section class="fade-in">
    <h2>Tools Used</h2>
    <div class="tags">
      <span class="tag blue">Airtable</span>
      <span class="tag green">Slack</span>
      <span class="tag purple">Relational Database Design</span>
      <span class="tag orange">QA Frameworks</span>
      <span class="tag gray">Content Design</span>
      <span class="tag pink">Instructional Design</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="divider"><hr/></div>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section>
    <div class="cta-box fade-in">
      <h2>Interested in this project?</h2>
      <p>I'd love to discuss how a similar system could work for your team.</p>
      <a href="index.html#contact" class="btn btn-primary">Get in Touch</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <footer>&copy; 2026 Sally May Saclauso. Built with care.</footer>
  <script>
    const observer=new IntersectionObserver(e=>{e.forEach(el=>{if(el.isIntersecting)el.target.classList.add('visible')})},{threshold:.1});
    document.querySelectorAll('.fade-in').forEach(el=>observer.observe(el));
  </script>
</body>
</html>
